# COGIC LIVE — environment template (no real secrets)
# Copy values into .env.local (local) or Vercel Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# Never commit real keys. Never enable mock flags on Vercel Production.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Core app / Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
COGIC_STREAM_PUBLIC_WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe (webhook is payment authority — never mark paid from browser redirect)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Registration pricing + credential session
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGISTRATION_FEE_CENTS=25000
REGISTRATION_CURRENCY=usd
COGIC_CREDENTIAL_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cron (Vercel Cron Bearer auth)
# Protects:
#   /api/cron/process-reminders
#   /api/cron/process-registration-credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRON_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Registration runtime boundary (DEFINE THE ENVIRONMENT BOUNDARY)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MUST remain false (or unset) in production / Vercel production.
# If USE_MOCK_REGISTRATION=true inside the production boundary, /api/health
# returns status=not_ready immediately (mockRegistrationDisabled=false).
# Sandbox mock mode is never production PASS (Law 24 / Law 25).
USE_MOCK_REGISTRATION=false

# Optional explicit boundary override used by runtime-mode assessment:
# COGIC_RUNTIME_ENV=development
# COGIC_RUNTIME_ENV=preview
# COGIC_RUNTIME_ENV=production

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security bypasses — must be unset/false for readiness
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LIVE_ACCESS_DEV_BYPASS=false
OPS_ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS=false
ATTENDEE_AUTH_OPEN=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting (recommended for production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REDIS_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_URL=
# RATE_LIMIT_REDIS_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner / admin
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMIN_EMAILS=owner@example.org

---

## Operator Smoke Test Checklist

Complete on the **target** Supabase + Vercel Production project before declaring Registration Hub production PASS.
Incomplete items = **BLOCKED — OPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED** (do not fake PASS).

- [ ] `USE_MOCK_REGISTRATION` is `false` or unset in Vercel **Production**
- [ ] `LIVE_ACCESS_DEV_BYPASS`, `OPS_ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS`, and `ATTENDEE_AUTH_OPEN` are unset/false in Production
- [ ] Migrations applied: `20260812010000` through `20260812060000`
- [ ] `GET /api/health` returns `"status":"ready"` and `"mockRegistrationDisabled":true`
- [ ] Attendee can save Step 1 primary draft (`save_registration_primary_draft`) and resume by `?step=`
- [ ] Free or paid submit path persists group members atomically (no partial multi-row writes)
- [ ] Registration webhooks receive signed `checkout.session.completed` and `checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded` with `checkout_type`, `registration_id`, `program_key`, `user_id`, `amount_cents`, Session id, and PaymentIntent id tracked
- [ ] `payment_intent.succeeded` remains routed for travel PaymentIntents; it is not registration redirect authority
- [ ] Paid path: Stripe Checkout → webhook → group `confirmed` (redirect alone does **not** confirm)
- [ ] `/register/review` resume copy matches pending vs stale vs webhook-processing modes
- [ ] Credential issuance succeeds OR a real `registration_credential_jobs` row is queued (no fake QR)
- [ ] Vercel Cron hits `/api/cron/process-registration-credentials` with `CRON_SECRET` and returns `{ ok: true }`
- [ ] Owner/operator profile correction uses allowlisted fields only (price/status rejected)
- [ ] Refund ledger table `registration_refund_operations` exists; no UI claims refund without Stripe evidence
- [ ] `registration_reconciliations` records action, outcome, actor, notes, Stripe identifiers/reference, and timestamp
- [ ] Preview-only: set `USE_MOCK_REGISTRATION=true`, verify `sandbox:true` structural responses, then reset false and confirm health readiness before promotion
- [ ] `npm run test:registration` and `npm run build` pass on the release commit
